Challenge Prompt: 

Turn complex, messy data into insights, answers, or actions. Qualified projects must use Elasticsearch and are judged on: Depth and creativity of the Elasticsearch implementation; Use of Jina models for embeddings; Use of Elastic Agent Builder and Workflows; Use of Elastic Cloud Serverless.

Our Approach: 
Rather than using Elasticsearch as a passive document store or text-only RAG database, we position it as the central Multimodal Episodic Memory & Cognitive Inference Engine deployed entirely on Elastic Cloud Serverless.
The system continuously streams unstructured, high-frequency, noisy data from two distinct physical sources: 8-channel EEG brainwave telemetry (band powers across Alpha, Beta, Theta, Gamma, and IMU motion) and synchronized POV video/audio.
Signal Ingestion & Indexing: When a physiological spike occurs (e.g., surprise, sudden cognitive engagement, or error-related potential), the event window is bundled with surrounding context and ingested into a dedicated cognitive-moments index on Elastic Cloud Serverless.
Jina Embedding Integration: Using the Elastic Inference API, each short video is embedded directly with Jina v5 Omni. Text queries use the same multimodal vector space, enabling cross-modal retrieval without requiring a transcript or a separately generated caption.
Hybrid & Vector Search: We implement hybrid search combining BM25 keyword matching with dense kNN vector search via Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF). Queries like "When was I startled while reading?" execute a vector similarity search against Jina embeddings, combined with a numerical filter on EEG confidence and frequency bands.
Elastic Workflows (Deterministic Signal Processing): We configure automated Elastic Workflows triggered on document ingest. The workflow normalizes real-time EEG band ratios against the user's historical rolling baseline, aggregates clustered events into continuous "Moments," and automatically classifies event severity.
Elastic Agent Builder (Conversational Memory Recall): We build an agent equipped with specialized Elasticsearch tools (search_moments_by_biometrics, correlate_eeg_visuals). Users can converse naturally with their cognitive memory agent—asking what caused cognitive load spikes, and navigating straight to the synchronized POV video playback in the Netflix-style viewer.



