IMPLEMENTED FIRST SLICE (2026-09-19)

- `hardware-demo/eegdemo/elastic_store.py` is the single Elastic Cloud boundary.
- Completed phone moments are embedded directly by Jina v5 Omni through Elastic Inference
  Service and indexed in `memorypalace-multimodal-moments` with a 1024-dimensional cosine vector.
- `GET /search?q=...` fuses BM25 and dense kNN with RRF and supports event/confidence filters.
- Explore translates its red/orange/yellow/green intensity bands into lower and upper
  `confidence` range filters inside both the BM25 and kNN branches. Time remains the default
  ordering, with an optional strongest-first view and a clickable full-session timeline.
- `/explore` uses the Elastic results and visibly identifies `ELASTIC · JINA V5 OMNI · HYBRID RRF`;
  it falls back to local text search when the sponsor service is unavailable.
- Only `ELASTICSEARCH_URL` and `ELASTIC_API_KEY` are required. The key remains server-side
  and is never committed, returned by `/status`, sent to the phone, or exposed to the browser.
- Local camera capture remains authoritative: an Elastic outage records an event but never
  blocks or discards the uploaded moment.

The live project endpoint is:
`https://my-vectordb-project-bece59.es.us-east4.gcp.elastic.cloud`

